message: "If you use this kit in research or a report, please cite it as below."
title: "DPDPA Engineering Kit"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "StateCheck Security"
    website: "https://statechecksecurity.com"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/statecheck-security/dpdpa-engineering-kit"
url: "https://statechecksecurity.com/dpdpa"
abstract: >-
  Tested code patterns for India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the
  DPDP Rules, 2025: consent records and receipts, breach detection and notification,
  field-level encryption, data residency, CI/CD privacy gates, threat-model mitigations and
  control mappings to ISO 27001, SOC 2 and NIST. Engineering patterns, not legal advice.
keywords:
  - DPDP Act
  - DPDPA
  - India
  - privacy engineering
  - consent
  - breach notification
  - encryption
  - policy as code
